 \section{Conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}
 The prescribed-extinction problem has a unit normalized supremum within finite compact two-layer reciprocal anisotropic dielectrics at one frequency and under arbitrary fixed positive upper material caps. The proof combines exact rotation factorization, uniform normalized aperture localization, and two finite-object continuity arguments. Each selected object retains the exact extinction target and strictly positive tensor loss, while strict optical-theorem nonattainment prevents equality for an individual body. This gives a precise resource-unrestricted answer to one formulation of OQ7; finite-resource optima and bandwidth remain separate questions.
 
